<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antalaotra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Antalaotra were Muslim, Swahili-speaking merchant communities of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, of mixed East African, Arab and Malagasy descent. From towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahajanga">Mahajanga</a> they traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, dealing in slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and cloth. They came under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> kingdom of Boina in the late 17th and 18th centuries but kept their own trade and religion.</p></div>
